From 07882593ec3840e278fd6c3c9aa3bd7babf18b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "opus-pr2-patch (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:05:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] verify: strict bytes/sha256/count checks, run before the
 archive commit

Proofs-lane finding, reproduced: update-lightning.yml committed data/history
(step 5, if: always()) without running `history.py verify`, and
verify_archive skipped the size and hash checks whenever a row lacked
bytes or sha256 (history.py:282,284); it never compared feature counts.

- verify_archive is strict: bytes and sha256 must be present and match;
  each file's feature count must equal its row/part count; count is null
  iff coverage none; count > 0 needs a path or parts. Ingest keeps the
  lenient check for untouched rows (v1 upgrade path unchanged).
- The archive step runs `history.py verify` right after ingest, so a bad
  archive makes steps.archive.outcome a failure.
- The archive commit stages data/history only when that outcome is
  success; otherwise it restores the last committed archive (checkout +
  clean) and commits status.json alone, which records the failure.

Tests (all fail before): test_verify_requires_bytes_and_sha256_and_matching_counts,
test_archive_step_runs_verify_after_ingest_and_fails_when_verify_fails,
test_failed_archive_step_commits_status_only_and_restores_the_archive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
